   summary="The meeting noted its appointment order and set how it will work: it will study the problems, readiness and limits of public transport in Khon Kaen, Udon Thani, Ubon Ratchathani and Nakhon Ratchasima provinces. The Office of Transport and Traffic Policy and Planning (OTP) described its master plan for public transport in 11 main regional cities, which covers all 4 provinces. In 2567 public transport made up on average 3.27 per cent of trips, with targets of 5 per cent in 2570, 10 per cent in 2575 and 20 per cent in 2580. The proposed model is low-floor electric buses running to a timetable every 10–30 minutes, a flat fare of 15 baht and a common ticket system. The state would invest in infrastructure such as bus stops, depots and charging stations, while private operators would provide the buses and run the service. The meeting raised points about the rights of existing route operators, the readiness of local governments, and state support for routes with few passengers, and heard about a bus service in Ubon Ratchathani province that carries about 10 passengers per trip on average. The meeting asked the Department of Land Transport and OTP to compile the status of existing routes and operating rights in the 4 provinces, to compare with the network OTP proposes, and to bring the Ubon Ratchathani information to the next meeting.",
